+<div class="th"><p><span class="lab">Theorem 45 (rigidity of the ancestor matrix), proved.</span> Let \(T\) be a caterpillar and \(S\) a tree with the same \(A\) and \(N\). For each size \(w\), the multiset of sizes of internal edges directly below the edges of size \(w\) is the same in \(S\) and \(T\). Non-pendant sizes occur at most twice (with two virtual incoming edges at a balanced edge), and only a size occurring twice can distribute differently. If its 2 edges have children of sizes \(\xi,\eta\) in \(T\) and both children lie under 1 edge in \(S\), that size contributes \(2(\xi-1)(\eta-1)\) to the difference, and
